## 8. Environment variables

```
DATABASE_URL
BETTER_AUTH_SECRET
ORIGIN
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET
APPLE_CLIENT_ID
APPLE_CLIENT_SECRET
YANDEX_CLIENT_ID
YANDEX_CLIENT_SECRET
OPENAI_API_KEY
OPENAI_MODEL
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
ANTHROPIC_MODEL
GEMINI_API_KEY
GEMINI_MODEL
AI_ROUTER_PROVIDER_ORDER
AI_ROUTER_TIMEOUT_MS
AI_ROUTER_MAX_RETRIES
AI_ROUTER_MAX_ATTEMPTS
REDIS_URL
JOB_STREAM_JWT_SECRET
PUBLIC_JOB_STREAM_URL
STREAM_CORS_ORIGIN
STREAM_RECONCILE_INTERVAL_MS
MAX_ACTIVE_STREAMS
MAX_ACTIVE_STREAMS_PER_USER
PLATFORM_AI_PROVIDER
PLATFORM_AI_KEY
AI_KEYS_ENCRYPTION_KEY
ADMIN_SECRET
```

`REDIS_URL` — atomic auth/API rate limiting, worker wake-ups, and SSE notifications; production web/worker/gateway require it. PostgreSQL remains authoritative for sessions and jobs. `JOB_STREAM_JWT_SECRET` — shared by web (stream-token) and gateway. `PUBLIC_JOB_STREAM_URL` — base URL of the gateway for browser `EventSource` (no trailing slash). `STREAM_CORS_ORIGIN` — exact gateway CORS origin in production (`*` is local-only).

**Railway:** per-service `railway.toml` under `apps/worker/` and `apps/job-stream-gateway/` (RAILPACK + `bun install` from repo root); UI Root directory = repo root, Config file = that path.

**Readiness:** all three services require Redis in production and validate the complete app migration ledger/checksums. Gateway streams periodically reconcile PostgreSQL so a lost Redis publication cannot leave a terminal job stream open indefinitely.

**Observability:** `@oryxel/runtime` emits vendor-neutral JSON logs for web, worker, and gateway. Correlate HTTP events by validated `requestId` and background-job lifecycles by `jobId`. Never log request bodies, query strings, user IDs, arbitrary exception messages, stack traces, or credentials.

Extend this list in **`memory.mdc`** and here when new features add secrets.

